-# RMN fix 1 of 3 -- black nametags (photon issue #569).
-# Iris maps ShaderKey.TEXT, TEXT_INTENSITY and TEXT_BG (nametag glyphs and the
-# nametag backdrop) to ProgramId.EntitiesTrans. Disabling that program makes Iris
-# fall back to ProgramId.Entities -> gbuffers_entities -> program/gbuffers_all_solid,
-# a deferred gbuffer program drawn with blend.gbuffers_entities = off. The backdrop
-# quad (vertex colour 0,0,0, alpha = background opacity) is drawn last with no depth
-# test, so it overwrites the glyph albedo in colortex1 with opaque black without
-# writing depth: deferred shading then paints black text, a black backdrop over
-# blocks and nothing at all over sky. Leaving the program enabled sends nametags to
-# program/gbuffers_all_translucent, forward-shaded into colortex13 and composited by
-# c1_blend_layers via
-# blend.gbuffers_entities_translucent.colortex13 = ONE ONE_MINUS_SRC_ALPHA ...
-#
-# Scope: this moves EVERY ShaderKey.ENTITIES_TRANSLUCENT draw -- all
-# RenderType.entityTranslucent* and itemEntityTranslucentCull geometry, not just
-# nametags -- from the deferred path into the forward translucent layer, which is
-# what upstream does on MC >= 26.01. Known consequences on this branch:
-#   * armor/item glint still writes colortex3 and is applied by d4 to colortex1, so
-#     glint on geometry that moved forward (enchanted translucent item entities) is
-#     applied to the background albedo instead of to the item.
-#   * translucent entities write depth before copyPreTranslucentDepth(), so where
-#     their forward alpha < 1 the background behind them is shaded at their depth.
-# The other three programs stay disabled and USE_SEPARATE_ENTITY_DRAWS stays
-# undefined, so none of the eleven USE_SEPARATE_ENTITY_DRAWS sites change behaviour.
+# RMN fix 1 (rmnfix2 revision, 2026-09-06) -- nametags (photon issue #569) and Voxy.
+# Photon v1.3 shipped Iris' separateEntityDraws for every Minecraft version; v1.3a/v1.3b
+# (commits 65704f6/90451cc) turned it off below MC 26.1 and disabled the four translucent
+# programs, which is what made nametags black on 1.21.1 (#569, PR #570 restores v1.3).
+# The first rmnfix only re-enabled gbuffers_entities_translucent, so every entityTranslucent
+# draw (player skins, items, armor stands, slime skins, horse markings, ETF emissive overlays,
+# nametags) became a forward-layer draw made BEFORE Iris' pre-translucent depth copy - and
+# c1_blend_layers' Voxy guard then erased those texels wherever Voxy LOD terrain or LOD water
+# was behind them ("aspects of entities go transparent"). This revision restores the full
+# v1.3 configuration instead (see the lines below and settings.glsl), removes that guard the
+# way Photon main did (commit 1fac270) and, with the ported Voxy, defers Voxy's translucent
+# LOD pass until after entities (program/voxy.json "deferTranslucentRendering").
 
-# Separate Entity Draws
-#if MC_VERSION < 260100
-program.world0/gbuffers_entities_translucent.enabled   = true
-program.world0/gbuffers_block_translucent.enabled      = false
-program.world0/gbuffers_particles.enabled              = false
-program.world0/gbuffers_particles_translucent.enabled  = false
-program.world1/gbuffers_entities_translucent.enabled   = true
-program.world1/gbuffers_block_translucent.enabled      = false
-program.world1/gbuffers_particles.enabled              = false
-program.world1/gbuffers_particles_translucent.enabled  = false
-program.world-1/gbuffers_entities_translucent.enabled  = true
-program.world-1/gbuffers_block_translucent.enabled     = false
-program.world-1/gbuffers_particles.enabled             = false
-program.world-1/gbuffers_particles_translucent.enabled = false
-#endif
+# photon_v1.3b-rmnfix2 (option B): Photon v1.3 behaviour - Iris draws translucent entities,
+# translucent block entities and translucent particles after the translucent terrain
+# (separateEntityDraws), so all four programs stay enabled on every Minecraft version.
+separateEntityDraws = true
 
